    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 42,
        "text": "Hi, Ben. You look worried. What's up?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "1d8768ec3c57be16d579ff9493d1e5c2d12499c20546e8ce4203f1c26e046304",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 48,
        "sourceEnd": 158,
        "text": "Oh, hi Mia. It's my new smart speaker. I think it's great, but my sister says it listens to everything we say.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "4a880191d34ab1161ecb45fb185224e3411c3f5217334689ba327d739bfb0ba7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 164,
        "sourceEnd": 311,
        "text": "Well, that's partly true. Smart speakers only listen after they hear a wake word, like 'Hey Assistant'. But they do record what you say after that.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "cc77c292dc65fdc0756e84f39c69a0eb0c3658394790bedd5d0a24de29995155",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 317,
        "sourceEnd": 374,
        "text": "So if I say 'Hey Assistant, play music', it records that?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "582f5bbb7838f8641c03dbb692df5a3d663996815ae69ebf18344405af282078",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 380,
        "sourceEnd": 532,
        "text": "Yes, it saves the command. But the company says it deletes the recording after it answers. The problem is that some recordings are kept for improvement.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "62907a219b456cc52da94b7faf71d1bdd24318c856cd30e748ba2e0527be6588",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 538,
        "sourceEnd": 614,
        "text": "That's a bit scary. I don't want strangers hearing my private conversations.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "52dc0a7b1328d66519b141ef50b16c491af0b9536f47a7b8bc83857aa4bd161a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 620,
        "sourceEnd": 739,
        "text": "I understand. You can turn off the microphone when you don't need it. And you can delete your voice history in the app.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "46a8312a2d8d792c5c5053863f898e0e40d1f895b432695a432b07b566775e02",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 745,
        "sourceEnd": 809,
        "text": "Really? I didn't know that. But what if I forget to turn it off?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "f4f98e01c19bdafc87b0df2e8626d44bf5adb2751e6791274189027dd4f381a4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 815,
        "sourceEnd": 922,
        "text": "Then you should check the privacy settings. You can set it to delete recordings automatically after a week.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "1354e6688e316cc83775b8ebe2396ebda5a8569d627eadb6279ae6ef3b821d6e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 928,
        "sourceEnd": 1025,
        "text": "That sounds better. But my sister also said the speaker might share my data with other companies.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "4cba714132900b4988fd0b7ef617633be7e6e6c3917fd011af5a0d09665ef370",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1031,
        "sourceEnd": 1144,
        "text": "That depends on the company's policy. You should read the privacy notice. If they share data, they must tell you.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "dc568c49d54812d21830e75713ccb346da1c01cb516b0e9265ddb4bfa5e5052e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1150,
        "sourceEnd": 1187,
        "text": "OK. I'll read it. But it's very long.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "96a0116b7ff940b387be9254b07b829aa5ee478427d0a8f00cf1943b6c9eb159",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1193,
        "sourceEnd": 1325,
        "text": "I know. Look for the parts about 'data sharing' and 'third parties'. If you can't find them, you can ask the company's support team.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "37df5436b2a8a37a023e46106713df5377db2d3b1a2efe905cccc3962a5d95cb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1331,
        "sourceEnd": 1370,
        "text": "Thanks, Mia. You know a lot about this.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "b35767cc0c936599854096b9e4fa0b519cd8b88daa38dcbcc636d478f4289e76",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1376,
        "sourceEnd": 1455,
        "text": "I read a lot about technology. But I'm not an expert. I just try to be careful.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "9e461a3ea6463648ef59606174c9411f7bf501839b70ef3926ebb4766bcfcd3b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1461,
        "sourceEnd": 1544,
        "text": "Me too. I think privacy is important. Maybe I'll write a short guide for my family.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "530ceaccd2506d87e14e518b24050bab01b7c3147ccfb5d8b7a5d4325cb19077",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1550,
        "sourceEnd": 1677,
        "text": "That's a good idea. You could include a checklist: turn off the microphone, delete old recordings, and read the privacy notice.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "fe5c38d2a7f8cfcac2a5038b48b8a1ce95eafe4a4b8220c48e97931dbce394bc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1683,
        "sourceEnd": 1718,
        "text": "I'll do that. Thanks for your help!",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-WilliamNeural",
        "textHash": "bab67d4af33d5e4680ad65842b4d9be28af93d66d47af1c2796e4a720e691135",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1724,
        "sourceEnd": 1779,
        "text": "You're welcome. Let me know if you have more questions.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-AU-NatashaNeural",
        "textHash": "dff106a9667c792fd704d07cf5584e79557319bfe07abeeed1156423b6e76a1d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
